1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,930
A business brief should become a document a
team can review, not a black box.

2
00:00:04,950 --> 00:00:13,204
This is Docentric Copilot: a quotation brief in, a
reviewable DOCX out, with schema, validation and version
history attached.

3
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:20,282
Here is a synthetic package with sample data, parser
diagnostics and a normalized field tree.

4
00:00:20,302 --> 00:00:25,829
The schema is typed, so every field the
document can bind has a type and a source.

5
00:00:25,849 --> 00:00:29,148
Nothing is invented from the prompt alone.

6
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:32,714
The brief is the only input.

7
00:00:32,734 --> 00:00:38,548
It says what the document must contain, and the planner
maps each requirement to the schema.

8
00:00:38,568 --> 00:00:44,472
Routing weighs that brief and recommends a provider, but a
recommendation is not execution.

9
00:00:44,492 --> 00:00:49,980
The live trace records the model that actually ran, and
the validation gate it passed.

10
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,476
You do not have to guess which model to use.

11
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:59,242
The benchmark runs a fixed set of cases through each
provider and records what came back.

12
00:00:59,262 --> 00:01:05,830
The table is read straight from the live report: valid
templates, latency, and what each valid template cost.

13
00:01:05,850 --> 00:01:09,492
Cost is derived from measured spend and
valid runs.

14
00:01:09,512 --> 00:01:15,532
It is an observation, not a significance claim, and the
slide keeps the caveats visible.

15
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:18,897
Download the document and open it.

16
00:01:18,917 --> 00:01:25,654
The preview and the LibreOffice render are independent
views of the same file, and each is labelled for what it
is.

17
00:01:25,674 --> 00:01:29,027
The preview checks content and field
binding.

18
00:01:29,047 --> 00:01:32,855
The LibreOffice page checks an independent
render.

19
00:01:32,875 --> 00:01:41,012
This is a LibreOffice rendering, not a Microsoft Word
fidelity claim, and not a claim about Docentric AX
compatibility.

20
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:44,207
Here is the defect.

21
00:01:44,227 --> 00:01:51,407
The description column is too narrow, so the text wraps
past the line budget, and the checker flags a text-fit
warning.

22
00:01:51,427 --> 00:01:59,701
Optimize layout applies typed changes to the template: it
rebalances the columns, widens the description and adjusts
the table font.

23
00:01:59,721 --> 00:02:04,480
The panel reruns the checks, and the after
render uses fewer lines.

24
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:08,803
The change is reviewable in the diff, not
hidden in a binary.

25
00:02:08,823 --> 00:02:13,204
This is a LibreOffice rendering, not Word
pagination.

26
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:16,885
Every edit creates an immutable version.

27
00:02:16,905 --> 00:02:22,695
Compare versions names each changed field, and Restore
version brings either revision back into the workspace.

28
00:02:22,715 --> 00:02:26,700
The diff and rollback are part of the
deliverable, not an afterthought.

29
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:30,396
A reviewer can see exactly what changed and
undo it.

30
00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:36,048
Docentric Copilot is open source on GitHub
under the Apache license.

31
00:02:36,068 --> 00:02:40,844
The demo, the benchmark and the evidence are
in the repository.

32
00:02:40,864 --> 00:02:44,972
Docentric AX compatibility: not tested.

